From Late {{inh|en|enm|hagis||haggis}}, from {{m|enm|hag}}, {{m|enm|haggen||to chop, cut, hack; to cut into}} (from {{der|en|non|hǫggva||to hew}}),<ref>{{R:Lexico|nodot=yes}}; {{R:MED Online|entry=haggen|pos=v|id=MED19773|accessdate=28 October 2017}}</ref> or from {{m|enm|hakken||to chop, hack; to dice, mince}} (from {{inh|en|ang|hēawan||to chop, hew; to dice, mince}}),<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=hakken|pos=v|id=MED19811|accessdate=28 October 2017}}</ref> both ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*kewh₂-||to hew; to beat, strike; to forge}}.<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=hagis|pos=n|id=MED19777|accessdate=28 October 2017}}</ref>

